  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.4.31 (forks 2.4.30) - FIX (CUDA, OpenCL, Velocity, WebGPU, WebGL, Wasm; silent wrong results): an unsigned division by a constant power of two was an arithmetic shift (4294967295u / 2u gave 4294967295); it is a logical shift now. FIX (OpenCL; silent wrong results): signed +, -, *, << and unary - wrap around as in .NET (they were undefined on overflow in OpenCL C and NVIDIA's compiler used that: a mask deleted, (x + y) < x folded to y < 0). PERF (CUDA): a division or remainder by a constant power of two is shifts and masks (the PTX assembler does not reduce it: a loop with x / 16 took 3.95 ms, 1.03 ms now). New tests on every backend: IntegerWraparound_*, DivisionByConstant_*. See CHANGELOG.md.",
